    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "We use the input type checkbox to define a checkbox button. Checkboxes allow us to select more than one option. For example,"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "html",
      "content": "1<form>\n2  <p>Choose your favorite animals:</p>\n3\n4  <input type=\"checkbox\" name=\"animal1\" value=\"hamster\" />\n5  <label>Hamster</label><br>\n6  \n7  <input type=\"checkbox\" name=\"animal2\" value=\"cat\" /> \n8  <label>Cat</label><br>\n9  \n10  <input type=\"checkbox\" name=\"animal3\" value=\"dog\" /> \n11  <label>Dog</label><br>\n12  \n13  <input type=\"submit\" value=\"Select one\" />\n14</form>"
    },
